# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plan 00201 (pingbus fix) and Plan 00194 Task 2.0c (bus messages injected): deploys the ccy
# launcher 3.98.7, which requires container 2.62, so the next ccy launch rebuilds the image
# with the pingbus whose target refusals name what was refused and who can be addressed, and
# whose watcher writes each team message into the session as an `agent-bus delivery`
# envelope instead of the "N pending, run pingbus recv" notice (plugin 1.2.0). Running ccy
# sessions keep their old image and pingbus until each is relaunched.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00194 Task 2.0c: reinstalls the host's member kit and pingbus (agent-bus-install), so
# `cc --teams` sessions and LXC members also get team messages delivered as envelopes, with
# plugin 1.2.0's skill. Homeserver and teams are unchanged. Then SPEC-inject.md section 7,
# H1-H7, in a relaunched `ccy --teams` session (and H4 measures the socket's largest message).
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# Redeploys ssh-suspend-guard with its startup trap and "started" log moved below the
# test cut marker. Host behaviour is unchanged; the deployed script matches the repo again.
playbooks/imports/play-prevent-ssh-suspend.yml
# Plan 00192 (ftp-camera port): the camera FTP play now builds ~/.local/bin/ftp-camera from
# src-go/cmd/ftp-camera (installing the Go toolchain first) in place of the bash script; the
# vsftpd config changes only in its comments, and the camera account and the hotspot profile
# are unchanged. After it runs,
# `ftp-camera --copy-preflight` printing the mount's RC address and one `ftp-camera --sort`
# prove the binary on the host (SPEC-ftp-camera.md section 7, H1-H5). A play with no vaulted
# ftp_camera_password still only installs the Go toolchain and ends.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-ftp-camera.yml
# Plan 00192 (ftp-camera port): the rclone play redeploys rclone-rc-auth.bash, whose comments no
# longer name the deleted bash ftp-camera; behaviour unchanged. Without it the deployed-drift
# check reports the old copy.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-rclone.yml
